      "content": "Append to an Empty Circular Linked List"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Like with a singly linked list, we first need to check if the list is empty. If it is, the new node becomes the head."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "head = new_node;"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "And its next pointer points to itself"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "new_node->next = head;"
    },
